409:%We give short overviews of the two types of recombination steps we use:
411:%    \item A \textbf{gravity move} is a single ReCom move that decomposes the union of two adjacent districts using a horizontal line. By continuity, one such line maintains the areas of the districts.
415:%    \item An \textbf{exchange sequence} consists of three ReCom moves. The 1st move recombines the red and green districts to create monochromatic green corridors by exchanging parts of the red and green districts. The 2nd move eliminates monochromatic green and some blue corridors, and the 3rd one re-establishes the ordering property. The second and third move of an exchange sequence are gravity moves.
