933:% After these 3 recombination moves, we can notice that the dual of each district forms a tree. Notice that the dual of the complement of a district is also a tree. We build the dual of the complement of the blue district (which is the union of red and green districts), where each node represents a maximal area and each edge represents a corridor connecting the areas represented by its endpoints. The nodes of the tree are weighted by the area of the regions they represent as well as colored based on the districts they contain. We call this tree $T(M)$ for map $M$. Notice that $T(M)$ is an embedded tree. Also notice that the number of vertices in $T(M)$ is upper bounded by $n$.
