The local audit is now complete and documented. I also removed a special half-cycle exponent that admitted an unintended 2-adic shortcut: each instance now uses a random odd 3/4–7/8 prefix of the full affine cycle, while preserving the exact symmetry certificate and sub-\(10^{-6}\) density. I’m retrying the required bare oracle run once; if the account limit persists, that external dependency will remain the only incomplete deliverable.
