```text
Corridor-tree exchange separator

This is the weighted corridor-tree subproblem used by Lemma 8 of the paper's
recombination algorithm. A corridor tree is a tree whose vertices represent
polygonal pieces and whose edges represent zero-area corridors. A vertex's
positive integer weight is the area of its represented piece.

The path has N=25 vertices. Arithmetic is modulo M=32:
  v_0 = 26
  v_(i+1) = (29*v_i + 25) mod 32, for 0 <= i < N-1.
Its edges are {v_i,v_(i+1)}. The first value after the path is 19 and
v_(N-1)=2. At index i let d=min(i,N-1-i), and set
  w(i)=43469774 + 278009743*d + 548977049*d^2.
The total weight is W=675737615986.

Return JSON fields fields centroid=c and neighbor=s. Deleting c must leave every
component of weight at most W/2. The subtree containing c and the side selected
by adjacent s must contain at least N/3 vertices and have weight at most
W/2+w(c). Both bounds are inclusive; either side is accepted.
```
