codex
The final audit found a substantive G4 issue in the draft: uniform oriented-edge guessing still included pairs that visibly violate the stated subtree-size/weight rules. Under the required structure-aware prior, the old `n=21` shipping level has density about \(3.6\times10^{-6}\), so it does not pass. I’m fixing the sampler to draw only from candidates satisfying every non-centroid rule and sliding the non-demo ladder to `n=23,24,25`; this keeps the two-label witness fixed while restoring honest guess resistance.
apply patch
