    \caption{(Top) Transformation of a map in $\mathcal{R}$ (a) into a map in the punctured square $\mathcal{S}$ (c). We first perform $O(k)$ ReCom moves to ``coat'' a weakly simple hole $H$ with a single district (b).
    The retract $\mathcal{H^*}$ maps a weak representation of a map in $\mathcal{S}$ into a weak representation of a map in $\mathcal{R}$.
    %The homotopy $\mathcal{H}$ contracts the hole $H$ into a point $p_H$ in the interior of $H$, giving the region previously occupied by $H$ to the magenta district. (Bottom) The inverse homotopy $\mathcal{H}^{-1}$ pushes the portions of the districts inside $H$ into corridors on $\partial H$.
    }
